  "worked_solution": "On the interval $(-5,8),$ we can choose a test point ${x}_{1}=1.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5 & =1+5=(+), \\\\ x-8 & =1-8=(-), \\\\ (x+5)(x-8) & =(+)\\times (-)=(-),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we fill in the table as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-5)$ | $(-5,8)$ | $(8,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x+5$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $x-8$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $(x+5)(x-8)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |",
